#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:410
msgid "Custom (set aspect ratio and radius)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:416
msgid "Pizza Border Color"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:417
msgid ""
"The thin line around the pizza image. Use a warm brown or orange to make it "
"look like a crust edge."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:423
msgid "Accent / Highlight Color"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:424
msgid ""
"The main color used for selected items, buttons, and highlights throughout "
"the builder. Pick something that matches your brand."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:431
msgid "Look & Feel"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:433
msgid ""
"Give the builder your brand's personality. Set your primary and secondary "
"brand colors, and choose a font family. These work alongside your chosen "
"template's own styling."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:438
msgid "Brand Primary Color"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:439
msgid ""
"Your main brand color — used for buttons, selected states, and highlights. "
"This should match the primary color on your website."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:445
msgid "Brand Secondary Color"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:446
msgid ""
"A supporting color — used for hover states, secondary buttons, and accents. "
"Often a darker or lighter shade of your primary color."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:452
msgid "Font Family"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:453
msgid ""
"The font used inside the builder. Leave blank to use your theme's default "
"font. To use a Google Font, enter its exact name (e.g. \"Lato\" or "
"\"Poppins\") — make sure the font is already loaded by your theme."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:455
msgid "e.g. Lato, Poppins, or leave blank"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:461
msgid "Builder Layout"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:463
msgid ""
"Control the order of the ingredient tabs and a couple of layout options. The "
"tab order determines the steps customers follow when building their pizza — "
"put the most important choices first."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:468
msgid "Tab Order"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsWizard.php:469
msgid ""
"List the ingredient categories in the order you want them to appear as tabs, "
"separated by commas. For example: crust, sauce, cheese, toppings, drizzle, "
"slicing. Leave blank for the default order."
msgstr ""

